INSERT INTO missionObjectives (missionID, briefingText) VALUES
(91009,'/h2> Acquire the 20,000 units of Augumene at the location I''ve given you. Now, there may be other folks looking to get this stuff too, so don''t go out there unprepared to defend yourself, okay? </span'),
(57840,'/h2> Take this soil to the destination so our science weenies can figure out how to grow stuff for us to eat. No lollygagging. </span'),
(57890,'/h2> Take this soil to the destination so our science weenies can figure out how to grow stuff for us to eat. No lollygagging. </span'),
(60000,'/h2> Planetary officials have asked me to bring in a team of mercenaries they''ve hired to deal with a terrorist threat. Your job is to keep them in line en route. </span'),
(60074,'/h2> A few unfortunate members of our corporation were kidnapped yesterday. I have reliable information that their kidnappers are close by. If you find the kidnappers, then deal with them appropriately and return their captives to me, dead or alive. </span'),
(60037,'/h2> A small fleet of unidentified frigates has attacked one of our remote communications outposts, killing and injuring dozens of our personnel. Those who survived the attack managed to pilot a high-speed shuttle to the nearest station. However, we have strong reason to believe that a team of assassins is en route to their location to eliminate them before they can pass along the information about the organization responsible for this attack. We need you to make all possible haste to their location and rescue the survivors before this hit team arrives. </span'),
(60001,'/h2> I accidentally sent a client the wrong set of drones because they never specified what type he needed. Take the right cargo to him. Hopefully he won''t ask too many questions. </span'),
(60041,'/h2> I accidentally sent a client the wrong set of drones because they never specified what type he needed. Take the right cargo to him. Hopefully he won''t ask too many questions. </span'),
(60022,'/h2> The daughter of a Caldari executive was kidnapped this morning by a group of slavers while she was on holiday. They are demanding we provide them a large quantity of our rarest and most expensive metal, quantrium, in exchange for her life. There is no time to mount a rescue operation, so our only choice is to provide this shipment immediately. We will deal with those criminals once the girl has been released to us. However, time is of the essence, and our primary mission now is to deliver this shipment to a transshipment station for further transportation to the slavers'' designated rendezvous point. </span'),
(60048,'/h2> The daughter of a Caldari executive was kidnapped this morning by a group of slavers while she was on holiday. They are demanding we provide them a large quantity of our rarest and most expensive metal, quantrium, in exchange for her life. There is no time to mount a rescue operation, so our only choice is to provide this shipment immediately. We will deal with those criminals once the girl has been released to us. However, time is of the essence, and our primary mission now is to deliver this shipment to a transshipment station for further transportation to the slavers'' designated rendezvous point. </span'),
(57841,'/h2> Deliver these crates of long-limb roes to the destination station. </span'),
(57842,'/h2> Deliver these crates of long-limb roes to the destination station. </span'),
(57891,'/h2> Deliver these crates of long-limb roes to the destination station. </span'),
(57899,'/h2> Deliver these crates of long-limb roes to the destination station. </span'),
(60082,'/h2> We''ve spotted a few Angel Cartel ships roaming near here. We believe that they are part of a reconnaissance force sent to scout for a weakness in security. We sent men out to intercept them, but none have returned. Another surveillance team caught sight of the pirates again recently, though. The Angels are led by an infamous captain, Jenmai Hirokan. Do not underestimate him! Many have done so in the past and have paid the ultimate price. I won''t keep you here any longer. I''m sure you''ll want to get going before we lose sight of Hirokan and his allies again. </span'),
(60083,'/h2> We''ve spotted a few Angel Cartel ships roaming near here. We believe that they are part of a reconnaissance force sent to scout for a weakness in security. We sent men out to intercept them, but none have returned. Another surveillance team caught sight of the pirates again recently, though. The Angels are led by an infamous captain, Jenmai Hirokan. Do not underestimate him! Many have done so in the past and have paid the ultimate price. I won''t keep you here any longer. I''m sure you''ll want to get going before we lose sight of Hirokan and his allies again. </span'),
(60084,'/h2> We''ve spotted a few Angel Cartel ships roaming near here. We believe that they are part of a reconnaissance force sent to scout for a weakness in security. We sent men out to intercept them, but none have returned. Another surveillance team caught sight of the pirates again recently, though. The Angels are led by an infamous captain, Jenmai Hirokan. Do not underestimate him! Many have done so in the past and have paid the ultimate price. I won''t keep you here any longer. I''m sure you''ll want to get going before we lose sight of Hirokan and his allies again. </span'),
(60002,'/h2> Due to a recent series of inspections by the regional mine monitoring commission, we have found it necessary to purchase a large quantity of the latest generation of environmentally-friendly drills and related equipment. In order to avoid financial penalties and the possible loss of our mining rights, that company must get these quite expensive new drills into the hands of the miners as soon as possible. If you can deliver this cargo to the station that serves as our logistical hub for this system, they can then have their own pilots transship them to the required planetary mining locations. </span'),
(60042,'/h2> Due to a recent series of inspections by the regional mine monitoring commission, we have found it necessary to purchase a large quantity of the latest generation of environmentally-friendly drills and related equipment. In order to avoid financial penalties and the possible loss of our mining rights, that company must get these quite expensive new drills into the hands of the miners as soon as possible. If you can deliver this cargo to the station that serves as our logistical hub for this system, they can then have their own pilots transship them to the required planetary mining locations. </span'),
(55186,'/h2> The the destination station manager has reported a lack of mono-cell batteries in their supply depot, a situation that could result in a temporary shutdown of the entire station. Deliver the batteries to them as quickly as possible. </span'),
(57910,'/h2> The the destination station manager has reported a lack of mono-cell batteries in their supply depot, a situation that could result in a temporary shutdown of the entire station. Deliver the batteries to them as quickly as possible. </span'),
(90000,'/h2> The the destination station manager has reported a lack of mono-cell batteries in their supply depot, a situation that could result in a temporary shutdown of the entire station. Deliver the batteries to them as quickly as possible. </span'),
(90032,'/h2> The the destination station manager has reported a lack of mono-cell batteries in their supply depot, a situation that could result in a temporary shutdown of the entire station. Deliver the batteries to them as quickly as possible. </span'),
(90053,'/h2> The the destination station manager has reported a lack of mono-cell batteries in their supply depot, a situation that could result in a temporary shutdown of the entire station. Deliver the batteries to them as quickly as possible. </span'),
(90074,'/h2> The the destination station manager has reported a lack of mono-cell batteries in their supply depot, a situation that could result in a temporary shutdown of the entire station. Deliver the batteries to them as quickly as possible. </span'),
(60003,'/h2> A friend and I are running a small holoreel bootlegging operation on the side. The shipments are bound for Syndicate, but I only need you to take them on to where my business partner is operating from. </span'),
(60043,'/h2> A friend and I are running a small holoreel bootlegging operation on the side. The shipments are bound for Syndicate, but I only need you to take them on to where my business partner is operating from. </span'),
(60025,'/h2> Our salvagers have built up a load of industrial-quality scrap metal to be used in ship building. I need you to take it to the reclamation facility so we can recover the useable parts. </span'),
(58057,'/h2> The Imperial Navy recently made a final attempt to scour the battlefield graveyard of The Battle of Vak-Atioth. This battle pitted our brave Navy against the Jovian enemy; however, due to a number of unforeseeable factors, we did not emerge victorious. The graveyard itself has been picked over for decades by scavengers and others seeking some quick isk. The Amarr ships sent to perform this duty were attacked by pirates, and only one ship eventually returned. But when it did, it brought with it a valuable icon of Amarr military history: a selection of data chips holding recordings of a small part of that legendary battle. We need these chips delivered to a distant station for proper cleaning and processing. </span'),
(58114,'/h2> The Imperial Navy recently made a final attempt to scour the battlefield graveyard of The Battle of Vak-Atioth. This battle pitted our brave Navy against the Jovian enemy; however, due to a number of unforeseeable factors, we did not emerge victorious. The graveyard itself has been picked over for decades by scavengers and others seeking some quick isk. The Amarr ships sent to perform this duty were attacked by pirates, and only one ship eventually returned. But when it did, it brought with it a valuable icon of Amarr military history: a selection of data chips holding recordings of a small part of that legendary battle. We need these chips delivered to a distant station for proper cleaning and processing. </span'),
(60004,'/h2> The Imperial Navy recently made a final attempt to scour the battlefield graveyard of The Battle of Vak-Atioth. This battle pitted our brave Navy against the Jovian enemy; however, due to a number of unforeseeable factors, we did not emerge victorious. The graveyard itself has been picked over for decades by scavengers and others seeking some quick isk. The Amarr ships sent to perform this duty were attacked by pirates, and only one ship eventually returned. But when it did, it brought with it a valuable icon of Amarr military history: a selection of data chips holding recordings of a small part of that legendary battle. We need these chips delivered to a distant station for proper cleaning and processing. </span'),
(55184,'/h2> I want these elite troops delivered to the destination for inspection. We hired them recently from an Amarrian security firm to work as guards on our transport vessels. Standard procedure requires that they be inspected for any possible diseases or mental disorders before they''re allowed on board. </span'),
(57911,'/h2> I want these elite troops delivered to the destination for inspection. We hired them recently from an Amarrian security firm to work as guards on our transport vessels. Standard procedure requires that they be inspected for any possible diseases or mental disorders before they''re allowed on board. </span'),
(90001,'/h2> I want these elite troops delivered to the destination for inspection. We hired them recently from an Amarrian security firm to work as guards on our transport vessels. Standard procedure requires that they be inspected for any possible diseases or mental disorders before they''re allowed on board. </span'),
(90033,'/h2> I want these elite troops delivered to the destination for inspection. We hired them recently from an Amarrian security firm to work as guards on our transport vessels. Standard procedure requires that they be inspected for any possible diseases or mental disorders before they''re allowed on board. </span'),
(90054,'/h2> I want these elite troops delivered to the destination for inspection. We hired them recently from an Amarrian security firm to work as guards on our transport vessels. Standard procedure requires that they be inspected for any possible diseases or mental disorders before they''re allowed on board. </span'),
(90075,'/h2> I want these elite troops delivered to the destination for inspection. We hired them recently from an Amarrian security firm to work as guards on our transport vessels. Standard procedure requires that they be inspected for any possible diseases or mental disorders before they''re allowed on board. </span'),
(60005,'/h2> I have a very special delivery that needs to be transported to the destination. The contents of the package are confidential, so do not even think of scanning it. The recipient will extract the package from your hangar at the destination as soon as you notify him that you''re ready, no questions asked. I promise to work double-overtime should you deliver this package for me today. </span'),
(60038,'/h2> I have a very special delivery that needs to be transported to the destination. The contents of the package are confidential, so do not even think of scanning it. The recipient will extract the package from your hangar at the destination as soon as you notify him that you''re ready, no questions asked. I promise to work double-overtime should you deliver this package for me today. </span'),
(60049,'/h2> I have a very special delivery that needs to be transported to the destination. The contents of the package are confidential, so do not even think of scanning it. The recipient will extract the package from your hangar at the destination as soon as you notify him that you''re ready, no questions asked. I promise to work double-overtime should you deliver this package for me today. </span'),
(60061,'/h2> I have a very special delivery that needs to be transported to the destination. The contents of the package are confidential, so do not even think of scanning it. The recipient will extract the package from your hangar at the destination as soon as you notify him that you''re ready, no questions asked. I promise to work double-overtime should you deliver this package for me today. </span'),
(57843,'/h2> As you know, we have a reputation for being a rowdy bunch and not the most civilized organization in the cluster, but sometimes my own men amaze even me. Yesterday the lads were responsible for showing a VIP a good time and making sure he was entertained, but just now I got a call from a local station manager who''s refusing to clean up the mess they made. I''m sending you over there with an army of janitors. No, I don''t want to hear about it. Just get going. </span'),
(57892,'/h2> As you know, we have a reputation for being a rowdy bunch and not the most civilized organization in the cluster, but sometimes my own men amaze even me. Yesterday the lads were responsible for showing a VIP a good time and making sure he was entertained, but just now I got a call from a local station manager who''s refusing to clean up the mess they made. I''m sending you over there with an army of janitors. No, I don''t want to hear about it. Just get going. </span'),
(60006,'/h2> A Nefantar House is relocating to a planet within the Republic, and we''ve had a tip-off that they''re working against us for someone in the Empire. We''ve planted surveillance nanobots in a shipment of materials for their planetside home; take it over to the depot. The logs will show nothing amiss. </span'),
(57833,'/h2> One commodity we all have a hard time living without is oxygen. One of our buyers is on a station that''s close to running out of air, so I want you to fly over to the destination and give them a bit more. </span'),
(57985,'/h2> One commodity we all have a hard time living without is oxygen. One of our buyers is on a station that''s close to running out of air, so I want you to fly over to the destination and give them a bit more. </span'),
(90002,'/h2> One commodity we all have a hard time living without is oxygen. One of our buyers is on a station that''s close to running out of air, so I want you to fly over to the destination and give them a bit more. </span'),
(90034,'/h2> One commodity we all have a hard time living without is oxygen. One of our buyers is on a station that''s close to running out of air, so I want you to fly over to the destination and give them a bit more. </span'),
(90055,'/h2> One commodity we all have a hard time living without is oxygen. One of our buyers is on a station that''s close to running out of air, so I want you to fly over to the destination and give them a bit more. </span'),
(90076,'/h2> One commodity we all have a hard time living without is oxygen. One of our buyers is on a station that''s close to running out of air, so I want you to fly over to the destination and give them a bit more. </span'),
(60076,'/h2> Ah, you, good to see you. To business. We''ve just detected a hidden Amarrian reconnaissance outpost nearby. I don''t need to explain the threat to you, do I? We must wipe them out before they are able to expand their operations further into our territory. If you can take care of this problem for me, you will be well rewarded. </span'),
(60079,'/h2> A Caldari pilot who has been helpful to the Empire in the past was ambushed by Gallente ships and managed to limp away to the safe haven of a station run by the Sisters of EVE. Go make sure that the lingering Gallente ship that is waiting for her to leave will not be a problem. </span'),
(60032,'/h2> I accidentally sent the wrong shipment over to another laboratory. I need to you take these frogs over; it''s the right shipment, this time, I''m positive! </span'),
(60054,'/h2> I accidentally sent the wrong shipment over to another laboratory. I need to you take these frogs over; it''s the right shipment, this time, I''m positive! </span'),
(60075,'/h2> Our counter-intelligence service has indicated that the Gallente Federal Intelligence Office has erected a covert listening post in the dungeon. While our communications are encrypted, the presence of Gallente intelligence operations in our space poses both an insult to Caldari sovereignty and an unacceptable risk to communications security. </span'),
(60007,'/h2> the agent''s corporation has a number of outposts in w-space systems, exploring what lies beyond known space. They''ve turned up some unusual pieces which I need you to take to a more extensive laboratory for identification. </span'),
(60044,'/h2> the agent''s corporation has a number of outposts in w-space systems, exploring what lies beyond known space. They''ve turned up some unusual pieces which I need you to take to a more extensive laboratory for identification. </span'),
(60115,'/h2> Our supporters in Amarr space have managed to smuggle out some slaves. I need you to go to the dungeon and destroy the Amarr pursuit team. </span'),
(60116,'/h2> The Amarr are threatening to attack the station in an effort to reclaim their slaves. I need you to transport them to another station where they will be safe should the Amarrians attack. </span'),
(60062,'/h2> The Amarr are still threatening to attack the station. Destroy their strike force. We read one dreadnought with them, though she seems to be playing support. Pay her no mind. We''ve got a little surprise in store for her. Watch for instructions after you clean up the rest. </span'),
(91016,'/h2> I hear there''s some Green Arisite that a bunch of people are looking to get their hands on. Now, I don''t know why they want it, but if they want it, I want it. You may have to hunt for it a bit; I hear the belt''s got a lot of big broken-up old asteroids floating around. Might be a little creepy, but it shouldn''t do you any harm, and I want that damn rock! </span'),
(57834,'/h2> An arms dealer passing through the system just sold us a cache of weapons. I need you to take it to the destination for me. Don''t worry, we''ve already acquired a permit for them, so you won''t have any trouble at customs. </span'),
(57986,'/h2> An arms dealer passing through the system just sold us a cache of weapons. I need you to take it to the destination for me. Don''t worry, we''ve already acquired a permit for them, so you won''t have any trouble at customs. </span'),
(90003,'/h2> An arms dealer passing through the system just sold us a cache of weapons. I need you to take it to the destination for me. Don''t worry, we''ve already acquired a permit for them, so you won''t have any trouble at customs. </span'),
(90035,'/h2> An arms dealer passing through the system just sold us a cache of weapons. I need you to take it to the destination for me. Don''t worry, we''ve already acquired a permit for them, so you won''t have any trouble at customs. </span'),
(90056,'/h2> An arms dealer passing through the system just sold us a cache of weapons. I need you to take it to the destination for me. Don''t worry, we''ve already acquired a permit for them, so you won''t have any trouble at customs. </span'),
(90077,'/h2> An arms dealer passing through the system just sold us a cache of weapons. I need you to take it to the destination for me. Don''t worry, we''ve already acquired a permit for them, so you won''t have any trouble at customs. </span'),
(55189,'/h2> A group of lads from the agent''s system have been requested by the faction army to the destination. I''ve agreed to their request, and I''d like you to carry it out. Deliver them to their destination, the faster the better. </span'),
(57912,'/h2> A group of lads from the agent''s system have been requested by the faction army to the destination. I''ve agreed to their request, and I''d like you to carry it out. Deliver them to their destination, the faster the better. </span'),
(90004,'/h2> A group of lads from the agent''s system have been requested by the faction army to the destination. I''ve agreed to their request, and I''d like you to carry it out. Deliver them to their destination, the faster the better. </span'),
(90036,'/h2> A group of lads from the agent''s system have been requested by the faction army to the destination. I''ve agreed to their request, and I''d like you to carry it out. Deliver them to their destination, the faster the better. </span'),
(90057,'/h2> A group of lads from the agent''s system have been requested by the faction army to the destination. I''ve agreed to their request, and I''d like you to carry it out. Deliver them to their destination, the faster the better. </span'),
(91000,'/h2> A huge asteroid has crashed into one of our stations. The station itself and most of the inhabitants are lost. This asteroid is particularly deadly in that it contains a huge quantity of Augumene, a rare and extremely toxic ore. We need someone to mine out the Augumene so rescue crews can go in there and retrieve the survivors. I''ve uploaded a bookmark to your People & Places databank; use it to find the crash site. Mine it all and bring the ore back to me. </span'),
(56919,'/h2> Turns out someone got the bright idea that if mining drones mine more ore, bigger drones would mine even more ore. This guy''s team slapped some mining drone''s AI into non-regulation heavy combat units and threw some mining lasers on. He even hacked the firmware so that the mining brains could control the weaponry, making some sort of self-sufficient mining machines. Now there''s a bunch of haywire drones zipping about this rare mineral that we want. Our guys in the lab need it for research, I guess. The drones aren''t even mining the rock, last I heard, but they have tried to bore through any ship we send out there.... It''s getting ridiculous. If you can, get out to the dungeon, neutralize the drones, and bring back all the Mercium; we''ll pay you well for your efforts. </span'),
(91010,'/h2> Turns out someone got the bright idea that if mining drones mine more ore, bigger drones would mine even more ore. This guy''s team slapped some mining drone''s AI into non-regulation heavy combat units and threw some mining lasers on. He even hacked the firmware so that the mining brains could control the weaponry, making some sort of self-sufficient mining machines. Now there''s a bunch of haywire drones zipping about this rare mineral that we want. Our guys in the lab need it for research, I guess. The drones aren''t even mining the rock, last I heard, but they have tried to bore through any ship we send out there.... It''s getting ridiculous. If you can, get out to the dungeon, neutralize the drones, and bring back all the Mercium; we''ll pay you well for your efforts. </span'),
(55188,'/h2> A relative of mine in the destination system just requested a special order of genetically enhanced livestock. I''d like you to deliver them to him in person; he''ll meet you on the destination. And keep a lid on this, will you? Some consumers, especially religious Amarrians, would boycott his wares if word got out he uses genetically enhanced animals. </span'),
(57913,'/h2> A relative of mine in the destination system just requested a special order of genetically enhanced livestock. I''d like you to deliver them to him in person; he''ll meet you on the destination. And keep a lid on this, will you? Some consumers, especially religious Amarrians, would boycott his wares if word got out he uses genetically enhanced animals. </span'),
(60033,'/h2> Several days ago, an internal security team identified a Gallente deep cover saboteur working at one of our clandestine shipyards producing the current generation of Widow-class Black Ops battleships. During a routine quality control check, the shipyard''s scientific team was shocked to discover a highly advanced nanite swarm that the saboteur had somehow introduced into the shipyard''s stockpile of advanced adhesives used to bond sensor-absorbing coatings to the hulls of our newly-constructed Widows. The effect of this harmful agent is to slowly erode this protective coating, thus increasing the ship''s sensor cross-section, making it much easier to detect and attack. Given the slow-acting nature of this particular breed of nanite, it is unlikely that this gradual loss of stealth capability would be noticeable under routine operating conditions, thus placing the ship and its crew at mortal risk when operating in hostile space. Therefore, we need you to immediately transport a large quantity of our new aerogel counteragent to a station for further distribution to the fleet. </span'),
(60055,'/h2> Several days ago, an internal security team identified a Gallente deep cover saboteur working at one of our clandestine shipyards producing the current generation of Widow-class Black Ops battleships. During a routine quality control check, the shipyard''s scientific team was shocked to discover a highly advanced nanite swarm that the saboteur had somehow introduced into the shipyard''s stockpile of advanced adhesives used to bond sensor-absorbing coatings to the hulls of our newly-constructed Widows. The effect of this harmful agent is to slowly erode this protective coating, thus increasing the ship''s sensor cross-section, making it much easier to detect and attack. Given the slow-acting nature of this particular breed of nanite, it is unlikely that this gradual loss of stealth capability would be noticeable under routine operating conditions, thus placing the ship and its crew at mortal risk when operating in hostile space. Therefore, we need you to immediately transport a large quantity of our new aerogel counteragent to a station for further distribution to the fleet. </span'),
(60087,'/h2> Destroy the Blood Raider installation and any ships trying to defend it. Bring back any tourists that are somehow still alive and in one piece. Remember, the Blood Raiders treat their victims like cattle to be drained and consumed. Therefore, search any cargo containers you discover. Each ship may have its own supply. </span'),
(91001,'/h2> My boss wants Banidine; something to do with manufacturing cheaper parts for refrigeration units or something. I don''t know. Point is, he''s made it my job to get the ore. And now I''m makin'' it your job. There''s a few Banidine rocks out at the dungeon, enough for 20,000 units, the scouts tell me. Go out there, mine it, bring it back. Should be easy enough, right? </span'),
(60026,'/h2> One of our planetside subsidiaries has recently lost a lot of farming equipment to a storm. I need you to take these parts to the assembly plant so we can recoup our losses. </span'),
(55191,'/h2> One of our transports flying through the destination broke down and requires immediate repairs. We''ve agreed to send him the spare parts he needs to complete the operation, and I''d like you to deliver the goods. If you''re fast he might even make it on time, so don''t tarry! </span'),
(57847,'/h2> One of our transports flying through the destination broke down and requires immediate repairs. We''ve agreed to send him the spare parts he needs to complete the operation, and I''d like you to deliver the goods. If you''re fast he might even make it on time, so don''t tarry! </span'),
(57901,'/h2> One of our transports flying through the destination broke down and requires immediate repairs. We''ve agreed to send him the spare parts he needs to complete the operation, and I''d like you to deliver the goods. If you''re fast he might even make it on time, so don''t tarry! </span'),
(57914,'/h2> One of our transports flying through the destination broke down and requires immediate repairs. We''ve agreed to send him the spare parts he needs to complete the operation, and I''d like you to deliver the goods. If you''re fast he might even make it on time, so don''t tarry! </span'),
(90005,'/h2> One of our transports flying through the destination broke down and requires immediate repairs. We''ve agreed to send him the spare parts he needs to complete the operation, and I''d like you to deliver the goods. If you''re fast he might even make it on time, so don''t tarry! </span'),
(90037,'/h2> One of our transports flying through the destination broke down and requires immediate repairs. We''ve agreed to send him the spare parts he needs to complete the operation, and I''d like you to deliver the goods. If you''re fast he might even make it on time, so don''t tarry! </span'),
(90058,'/h2> One of our transports flying through the destination broke down and requires immediate repairs. We''ve agreed to send him the spare parts he needs to complete the operation, and I''d like you to deliver the goods. If you''re fast he might even make it on time, so don''t tarry! </span'),
(90078,'/h2> One of our transports flying through the destination broke down and requires immediate repairs. We''ve agreed to send him the spare parts he needs to complete the operation, and I''d like you to deliver the goods. If you''re fast he might even make it on time, so don''t tarry! </span'),
(90006,'/h2> I need you to run over to the destination and drop off these electronic parts. The Chief Technical Operator there contacted me regarding the discovery of a major defect in their primary reactor, and they don''t have the parts on hand to repair it. </span'),
(90038,'/h2> I need you to run over to the destination and drop off these electronic parts. The Chief Technical Operator there contacted me regarding the discovery of a major defect in their primary reactor, and they don''t have the parts on hand to repair it. </span'),
(90059,'/h2> I need you to run over to the destination and drop off these electronic parts. The Chief Technical Operator there contacted me regarding the discovery of a major defect in their primary reactor, and they don''t have the parts on hand to repair it. </span'),
(90079,'/h2> I need you to run over to the destination and drop off these electronic parts. The Chief Technical Operator there contacted me regarding the discovery of a major defect in their primary reactor, and they don''t have the parts on hand to repair it. </span'),
(90007,'/h2> It just so happens that we''re opening some new clubs over in the destination. The problem is that the talent has gotten stranded here, and has to be over to the station for the grand opening. You probably know the rest. It''s important that this be taken care of soon, so we''re offering a substantial reward to anyone who wants to take the job. Remember to move the dancers to your cargo hold before departure. </span'),
(91002,'/h2> We''ve determined that the asteroid that collided with the station was composed of Augumene, which is particularly deadly in that it is a rare and extremely toxic ore. We need someone to mine out the Augumene safely from a starship. More than that, others may be coming for the Augumene. We can''t recover all the sensitive material from the wreckage of the base in time, and a blockade would tip our hand. The only solution is to mine out the Augumene ourselves. We want you to go out and retrieve all of the Augumene from the site. And hurry. I''ve uploaded a bookmark to your People & Places databank; use it to find the crash site and then mine all the Augumene and bring the ore back to me. </span'),
(56924,'/h2> There''s a field of Azure Ice at the dungeon. I want to sell it to some less-than-brilliant colonists. It''s not as good as Blue Ice, but the they won''t know the difference. Bring me back, oh, 20 blocks of it. I''ll split the profit with you. You will need an Ice Harvester module to complete this mission. Also, be aware that this amount of raw Azure Ice may require multiple trips unless you have a large amount of cargo space. </span'),
(91017,'/h2> There''s a field of Azure Ice at the dungeon. I want to sell it to some less-than-brilliant colonists. It''s not as good as Blue Ice, but the they won''t know the difference. Bring me back, oh, 20 blocks of it. I''ll split the profit with you. You will need an Ice Harvester module to complete this mission. Also, be aware that this amount of raw Azure Ice may require multiple trips unless you have a large amount of cargo space. </span'),
(57835,'/h2> It''s tough to quit smoking when you''ve got a warehouse full of cigarettes within arm''s reach. Take every crate of that crap you can find in that warehouse over to the destination and leave it there. Quickly, before I change my mind! </span'),
(57987,'/h2> It''s tough to quit smoking when you''ve got a warehouse full of cigarettes within arm''s reach. Take every crate of that crap you can find in that warehouse over to the destination and leave it there. Quickly, before I change my mind! </span'),
(90008,'/h2> It''s tough to quit smoking when you''ve got a warehouse full of cigarettes within arm''s reach. Take every crate of that crap you can find in that warehouse over to the destination and leave it there. Quickly, before I change my mind! </span'),
(57288,'/h2> We recently found a number of new mining fields in adjacent systems, and the usual assortment of pirate trash has come out of the woodwork to exploit it. We''ll need them mined soon because even those thieving bastards have friends in places high enough to put the legal status of these sites in doubt. For some reason they''ve taken an interest even in Banidine, too, and we''ll need to find out why; all my workers are busy with the more profitable fields, but I''m not taking any chances. I''m uploading a bookmark to your People & Places databank; it shows the location of a Banidine mining operation. I need you to head out there and mine all the Banidine. Should be 18,000 units, my foreman tells me. Once we''ve made an undisputed claim, we''re free to mine there again without interference, and I''ll provide you with a little something for your trouble. </span'),
(91005,'/h2> We recently found a number of new mining fields in adjacent systems, and the usual assortment of pirate trash has come out of the woodwork to exploit it. We''ll need them mined soon because even those thieving bastards have friends in places high enough to put the legal status of these sites in doubt. For some reason they''ve taken an interest even in Banidine, too, and we''ll need to find out why; all my workers are busy with the more profitable fields, but I''m not taking any chances. I''m uploading a bookmark to your People & Places databank; it shows the location of a Banidine mining operation. I need you to head out there and mine all the Banidine. Should be 18,000 units, my foreman tells me. Once we''ve made an undisputed claim, we''re free to mine there again without interference, and I''ll provide you with a little something for your trouble. </span'),
(60080,'/h2> In order to maximize the element of surprise for our raid, all enemy pickets and patrol ships must be destroyed. Go to the assigned location in the dungeon and destroy all the ships you find there. Beware of enemy reinforcements! </span'),
(56916,'/h2> the agent''s corporation wants a massive shipment of Augumene right away, so we need you to get out there and bring some back. I''ve been looking for a miner who''s experienced enough, with the right kind of ship, and maybe you fit the bill. Time is critical on this one. There''s a big bonus for you if you can bring it in fast enough. Pirates and claimjumpers abound in these parts, so you should also be prepared to defend your ship from such scavengers. Finally, this amount of raw Augumene ore may require multiple trips unless you have a Hulk or a similarly large hauler for the job. </span'),
(91011,'/h2> the agent''s corporation wants a massive shipment of Augumene right away, so we need you to get out there and bring some back. I''ve been looking for a miner who''s experienced enough, with the right kind of ship, and maybe you fit the bill. Time is critical on this one. There''s a big bonus for you if you can bring it in fast enough. Pirates and claimjumpers abound in these parts, so you should also be prepared to defend your ship from such scavengers. Finally, this amount of raw Augumene ore may require multiple trips unless you have a Hulk or a similarly large hauler for the job. </span'),
(55193,'/h2> A spate of engine failures and system crashes at a client firm in the destination has forced them to come to us for more coolants. We have some extras available, which I''d like you to deliver. Get it done in time, before their manager suffers a nervous breakdown, to earn your bonus. </span'),
(57915,'/h2> A spate of engine failures and system crashes at a client firm in the destination has forced them to come to us for more coolants. We have some extras available, which I''d like you to deliver. Get it done in time, before their manager suffers a nervous breakdown, to earn your bonus. </span'),
(90009,'/h2> A spate of engine failures and system crashes at a client firm in the destination has forced them to come to us for more coolants. We have some extras available, which I''d like you to deliver. Get it done in time, before their manager suffers a nervous breakdown, to earn your bonus. </span'),
(90039,'/h2> A spate of engine failures and system crashes at a client firm in the destination has forced them to come to us for more coolants. We have some extras available, which I''d like you to deliver. Get it done in time, before their manager suffers a nervous breakdown, to earn your bonus. </span'),
(90060,'/h2> A spate of engine failures and system crashes at a client firm in the destination has forced them to come to us for more coolants. We have some extras available, which I''d like you to deliver. Get it done in time, before their manager suffers a nervous breakdown, to earn your bonus. </span'),
(90080,'/h2> A spate of engine failures and system crashes at a client firm in the destination has forced them to come to us for more coolants. We have some extras available, which I''d like you to deliver. Get it done in time, before their manager suffers a nervous breakdown, to earn your bonus. </span'),
(57997,'/h2> You have established yourself as a trustworthy client of the agent''s corporation. I have some corporate documents for you to deliver to the destination. You have 24 hours to get this done; that should be no problem for someone as yourself, right? I assure you the reward will be well worth the effort. </span'),
(90010,'/h2> You have established yourself as a trustworthy client of the agent''s corporation. I have some corporate documents for you to deliver to the destination. You have 24 hours to get this done; that should be no problem for someone as yourself, right? I assure you the reward will be well worth the effort. </span'),
(60088,'/h2> Within the next week the Gallente Federation will officially claim sovereignty over the the dungeon , citing a recent worker''s riot as proof of “a desire for democracy”. The Federation has moved a division of their Navy into the system, and if we don''t forcibly push them out soon the riots could escalate further. Slip past the Navy forces from their rear flank and destroy the Gallente command ship and its escorts.. This will throw the rest of the division into disarray momentarily, and at that point, the Caldari Navy will move in. </span'),
(60021,'/h2> Against my better judgment, I''ve been asked to order several sets of educational packages of the Amarr Scriptures for the children of families who have been released by the Empire. It leaves a sour taste in the mouth, but maybe we can use the teaching materials to our own ends. </span'),
(60046,'/h2> Against my better judgment, I''ve been asked to order several sets of educational packages of the Amarr Scriptures for the children of families who have been released by the Empire. It leaves a sour taste in the mouth, but maybe we can use the teaching materials to our own ends. </span'),
(57062,'/h2> I''d like you to fly to the dungeon posing as a freelance miner; while you''re out there, we''ll have a reconnaissance module installed in your ship. Go to the asteroid field that we''ve entered into your NeoCom and mine 2,000 units of Scordite. Of course we''ll reimburse you generously for your time and for the ore – the mining mission is just a cover for the recon mission. While you''re mining, the recon module will be scanning the region and monitoring Amarrian activity around the system. You''ll never even notice it''s there. Once you''ve finished, head back here and we''ll recover the recon unit, take the ore, and reward you for your efforts. I''d advise caution in the area as well: There are lots of miners around, but the Amarr will be suspicious of any vessel that originates from Republic space. </span'),
(57063,'/h2> I''d like you to fly to the dungeon posing as a freelance miner; while you''re out there, we''ll have a reconnaissance module installed in your ship. Go to the asteroid field that we''ve entered into your NeoCom and mine 2,000 units of Scordite. Of course we''ll reimburse you generously for your time and for the ore – the mining mission is just a cover for the recon mission. While you''re mining, the recon module will be scanning the region and monitoring Amarrian activity around the system. You''ll never even notice it''s there. Once you''ve finished, head back here and we''ll recover the recon unit, take the ore, and reward you for your efforts. I''d advise caution in the area as well: There are lots of miners around, but the Amarr will be suspicious of any vessel that originates from Republic space. </span'),
(60089,'/h2> A group of Ammatar "nationals" in a small outpost out in the dungeon claim that they were beaten up by our security guards and then arrested on trumped-up charges. The Amarr Empire has dispatched a fleet to blockade the outpost; they are demanding that the prisoners be turned over to them. We''re in a no-win situation: If we hold the Nefantar, the Amarr fleet will bombard the station and force a confrontation, but if we turn them over it will be seen as a sign of weakness. We need to raise the blockade, while at the same time avoiding direct official intervention in the situation. Fly to the dungeon, take out the fleet that is amassing there. </span'),
(55208,'/h2> The greenhouses at the destination need a delivery of fertile soil. Take these crates and deliver them, would you? Thanks. Have an excellent day! </span'),
(57920,'/h2> The greenhouses at the destination need a delivery of fertile soil. Take these crates and deliver them, would you? Thanks. Have an excellent day! </span'),
(90011,'/h2> The greenhouses at the destination need a delivery of fertile soil. Take these crates and deliver them, would you? Thanks. Have an excellent day! </span'),
(90040,'/h2> The greenhouses at the destination need a delivery of fertile soil. Take these crates and deliver them, would you? Thanks. Have an excellent day! </span'),
(90061,'/h2> The greenhouses at the destination need a delivery of fertile soil. Take these crates and deliver them, would you? Thanks. Have an excellent day! </span'),
(90081,'/h2> The greenhouses at the destination need a delivery of fertile soil. Take these crates and deliver them, would you? Thanks. Have an excellent day! </span'),
(60090,'/h2> Stop the dissidents'' fleet by destroying every last one of them. </span'),
(58079,'/h2> Amarr scientists, working at a clandestine engineering laboratory in a nearby system may have developed the hardest metal yet known to science, known as Ditanium. The potential applications for warfare, specifically, in hardening our warships, is simply too tempting to pass up. Therefore, the full weight of the Amarr military science machine is waiting eagerly for the results of the pending tests, in which the Ditanium plates will be affixed to a specially modified frigate for flight testing. Therefore, we need you to deliver a large quantity of these plates to a nearby station where it will be transshipped to a military shipyard for fitting to the Punisher testbed ship. </span'),
(58350,'/h2> Amarr scientists, working at a clandestine engineering laboratory in a nearby system may have developed the hardest metal yet known to science, known as Ditanium. The potential applications for warfare, specifically, in hardening our warships, is simply too tempting to pass up. Therefore, the full weight of the Amarr military science machine is waiting eagerly for the results of the pending tests, in which the Ditanium plates will be affixed to a specially modified frigate for flight testing. Therefore, we need you to deliver a large quantity of these plates to a nearby station where it will be transshipped to a military shipyard for fitting to the Punisher testbed ship. </span'),
(60008,'/h2> Amarr scientists, working at a clandestine engineering laboratory in a nearby system may have developed the hardest metal yet known to science, known as Ditanium. The potential applications for warfare, specifically, in hardening our warships, is simply too tempting to pass up. Therefore, the full weight of the Amarr military science machine is waiting eagerly for the results of the pending tests, in which the Ditanium plates will be affixed to a specially modified frigate for flight testing. Therefore, we need you to deliver a large quantity of these plates to a nearby station where it will be transshipped to a military shipyard for fitting to the Punisher testbed ship. </span'),
(60009,'/h2> There has been an uprising at one of our slave Labor Reeducation Centers, or LRCs, near a rather large ore mine. The slaves are almost wholly Minmatar, so we cannot afford to have this incident continue for even one more day. The longer it goes on, the greater the chances that some reporter or news agency will get wind of this and splash the story all over the region. Given that the Minmatar Republic may feel compelled to take action to aid their brethren, this can only lead to dire consequences. That, of course, is unacceptable. We do have a plan in place, however, that should end this uprising before it has a chance to truly take root. We need you to transport a large contingent of Riot Interdiction Team (RIT) personnel to a designated station. From there the assembled security teams will join up and embark a small fleet of frigates and cruisers to race to the prison, where they will use all necessary force to terminate this uprising before it gets completely out of control. </span'),
(56875,'/h2> We''ve found a conglomeration of Augumene asteroids nearby. The ore''s not much good to anyone due to the exorbitant cost of reprocessing, of course, but a couple of our scientists are interested in doing some research on such a rare substance. In any case, hopefully you''ve been around the block enough times that you can find the ore and bring it in. </span'),
(91006,'/h2> We''ve found a conglomeration of Augumene asteroids nearby. The ore''s not much good to anyone due to the exorbitant cost of reprocessing, of course, but a couple of our scientists are interested in doing some research on such a rare substance. In any case, hopefully you''ve been around the block enough times that you can find the ore and bring it in. </span'),
(56915,'/h2> A recent survey scan of the dungeon reveals a big deposit of Banidine ore. We were content to leave it alone at first, but then we saw swarms of drones in the area. They seem to be making their way through the asteroid fields there in a hurry. They haven''t stumbled on the Banidine yet, but it''s only a matter of time. We want you to get to the ore before they do. I won''t lie to you; it''s going to be close. You may even have to fight a few of them off, so be careful. </span'),
(91012,'/h2> A recent survey scan of the dungeon reveals a big deposit of Banidine ore. We were content to leave it alone at first, but then we saw swarms of drones in the area. They seem to be making their way through the asteroid fields there in a hurry. They haven''t stumbled on the Banidine yet, but it''s only a matter of time. We want you to get to the ore before they do. I won''t lie to you; it''s going to be close. You may even have to fight a few of them off, so be careful. </span'),
(57850,'/h2> A few colleagues of mine are on an assignment in the destination and requested a batch of transmitters which they need for a particular task. I need them delivered there A.S.A.P. You''re up for the job, I presume? </span'),
(57880,'/h2> A few colleagues of mine are on an assignment in the destination and requested a batch of transmitters which they need for a particular task. I need them delivered there A.S.A.P. You''re up for the job, I presume? </span'),
(60047,'/h2> Following a string of suicide terrorist attacks yesterday, we managed to capture a high ranking member of their organization. Interrogations have revealed, however, that a devastating viral weapon, based on nanotechnology, is already in place and primed for release. We need you to deliver the only known countermeasure to this agent, manportable electromagnetic weapons. If we are successful, these weapons could eradicate the virus before it has a chance to spread and infect the entire station. </span'),
(60010,'/h2> Suicide terrorists have been attacking and destroying our commercial convoys as they have passed through their usual transit zones, despite the presence of heavy security escort vessels. A communications intercept, partially decoded, indicates that these individual intend to step up the level of their attacks by targeting the stations themselves. While we can defend against some of these attackers, based on analysis of their previous attack profiles, we have never had to defend against pilots and ships who fully intend to die by throwing themselves against us without regard for their own lives. Tactical analysis indicates that they will get through our defense and may cause catastrophic damage, likely killing hundreds if not thousands of our civilian workforce and their families. We need you to help us evacuate them immediately! </span'),
(60091,'/h2> A rogue drone infestation in the the dungeon system is causing problems and needs to be taken care of. </span'),
(60092,'/h2> A high-ranking Gallente officer has experienced a religious conversion and wants to defect to Amarr. This man, Admiral Meledier, has apparently arranged to lead a reconnaissance foray into our space and is holed up in an old outpost in the dungeon. Get out there and extract him from the rendezvous point. </span'),
(80076,'/h2> All the carnage you''ve inflicted on our enemies has caught the attention of a SARO pilot, Treonis. Taking you out is her bid at a promotion. My superiors want to see you handle this situation alone. Treonis is waiting for you by an abandoned colony in the dungeon. Destroy her, and the blueprint is yours. </span'),
(56929,'/h2> War is one of the biggest boons to business you could hope for. It''s a hungry giant that will eat anything you can throw at it. And the thing is, if you don''t feed it, it will just eat you…. But if you feed it well? Oh, the rewards. Public recognition, sure, but the contracts, the contracts, you! That''s where the real ISK is. And we''re going to get those contracts. Oh, yes. But first we need minerals. Right now, it seems the giant on our doorstep wants Oeryl, and we''re going to give it to him. There''s a deposit out at the dungeon. Bring back all 5,600 units of the stuff and I''ll make sure you get your share of the reward. </span'),
(91018,'/h2> War is one of the biggest boons to business you could hope for. It''s a hungry giant that will eat anything you can throw at it. And the thing is, if you don''t feed it, it will just eat you…. But if you feed it well? Oh, the rewards. Public recognition, sure, but the contracts, the contracts, you! That''s where the real ISK is. And we''re going to get those contracts. Oh, yes. But first we need minerals. Right now, it seems the giant on our doorstep wants Oeryl, and we''re going to give it to him. There''s a deposit out at the dungeon. Bring back all 5,600 units of the stuff and I''ll make sure you get your share of the reward. </span'),
(57851,'/h2> I''ve been ordered by the government to have these fertilizers delivered to the destination, from where they''ll be dispersed to nearby bio-domes. Quite a mundane job but one that needs to be done. Obviously I''d like you to do the honors of making the delivery, so here you go. </span'),
(57881,'/h2> I''ve been ordered by the government to have these fertilizers delivered to the destination, from where they''ll be dispersed to nearby bio-domes. Quite a mundane job but one that needs to be done. Obviously I''d like you to do the honors of making the delivery, so here you go. </span'),
(60081,'/h2> A Caldari envoy is soliciting our assistance for his particular area of space. However, his transport ship is poorly guarded. Meet him at the dungeon and escort him the rest of the way here. </span'),
(60011,'/h2> We have reason to believe that a small team of Gallente saboteurs has managed to destroy one of our new – and not yet fully operational – Command Centers on a nearby ice planet. These facilities are critical elements in our overall plan to dominate the planet such that we can then exploit the vast and lucrative materials that we have identified there in abundance. We need you to deliver a large complement of Arctic Warfare Marines to a forward station so that they can then be transferred down to provide the security we so desperately need. Their massive amounts of equipment will be brought in on other ships, so we need you to deliver these men safely and securely – everything depends on their safe arrival. </span'),
(60028,'/h2> We have reason to believe that a small team of Gallente saboteurs has managed to destroy one of our new – and not yet fully operational – Command Centers on a nearby ice planet. These facilities are critical elements in our overall plan to dominate the planet such that we can then exploit the vast and lucrative materials that we have identified there in abundance. We need you to deliver a large complement of Arctic Warfare Marines to a forward station so that they can then be transferred down to provide the security we so desperately need. Their massive amounts of equipment will be brought in on other ships, so we need you to deliver these men safely and securely – everything depends on their safe arrival. </span'),
(60050,'/h2> We have reason to believe that a small team of Gallente saboteurs has managed to destroy one of our new – and not yet fully operational – Command Centers on a nearby ice planet. These facilities are critical elements in our overall plan to dominate the planet such that we can then exploit the vast and lucrative materials that we have identified there in abundance. We need you to deliver a large complement of Arctic Warfare Marines to a forward station so that they can then be transferred down to provide the security we so desperately need. Their massive amounts of equipment will be brought in on other ships, so we need you to deliver these men safely and securely – everything depends on their safe arrival. </span'),
(60093,'/h2> Ah, you, I''m glad to see you received my mail. I have something that requires complete discretion. It''s entirely legal of course, but this will need to be kept quiet all the same. You''ve proven yourself trustworthy so if you want the assignment I''ll hand it over to you. During a routine system scan, some of my people stumbled upon something that may be a significant archaeological find. I can''t just call in anyone to confirm it, though, that would risk a leak. I don''t want anyone else claiming this discovery as their own, especially if it turns out to be a lucrative one. What we could do is rig your vessel''s camera drones to relay a live feed of the site back to me and my people. From there, we would be able to direct you around the area to observe places of interest. What you relay back could help us confirm or disprove our earlier findings. The site is in the dungeon, so you wouldn''t be travelling very far to investigate, either. The only problem my scouts reported was a light pirate presence. I''m sure you can deal with a few Guristas. Not the usual assignment I know, but one of potentially great importance…and profit. It would be ideal if we could rely on capsuleer assistance for this. </span'),
(57852,'/h2> I''ve got some stragglers here that claim they were raided by pirates and picked up by a transport vessel on its way here. I''ve decided to be charitable. Take them to the destination, but make sure you get there before the prisoner transport leaves for the slave camps. </span'),
(57904,'/h2> I''ve got some stragglers here that claim they were raided by pirates and picked up by a transport vessel on its way here. I''ve decided to be charitable. Take them to the destination, but make sure you get there before the prisoner transport leaves for the slave camps. </span'),
(57854,'/h2> Everything is overflowing with garbage. I want you to take it to the destination. I''ve done some fixing on the documents. They think they''re getting luxury foodstuffs. You might want to get out of there before they open up the crates. </span'),
(57905,'/h2> Everything is overflowing with garbage. I want you to take it to the destination. I''ve done some fixing on the documents. They think they''re getting luxury foodstuffs. You might want to get out of there before they open up the crates. </span'),
(56934,'/h2> I need pain medications badly. I can''t just wait for the next delivery. I need to produce my own drugs. For that I''m going to need Gamboge Cytoserocin. I heard a smuggler say there was a pocket at the dungeon. Go there, and bring back everything you can. I''ll try to make it worth your while. You need to fit a Gas Cloud Harvester to complete this mission. </span'),
(60094,'/h2> A maintenance team assigned to a top secret acceleration gate in the dungeon has stopped transmitting progress reports. As this gate leads to one of our new listening outposts, alarm rang out in military circles. Travel to the acceleration gate. Destroy any hostiles. Use the acceleration gate and check on the outpost. If the outpost''s location has been compromised, you are ordered to eliminate the hostiles and then destroy the gate. You must ensure that the enemy cannot return to the exact location of our outpost. </span'),
(56928,'/h2> We need a big shipment of Geodite crystals for a client of ours, some gemology lab. These gemologists figure they might be able to get some decent stones out of it and make a bit of profit that way. Whatever. They want to pay for it, so it''s all good by me. And you''ll get your cut, don''t worry. Geodite takes up a lot of room: You''re going to need a big cargo hold, or you''ll have to make several trips. </span'),
(91019,'/h2> We need a big shipment of Geodite crystals for a client of ours, some gemology lab. These gemologists figure they might be able to get some decent stones out of it and make a bit of profit that way. Whatever. They want to pay for it, so it''s all good by me. And you''ll get your cut, don''t worry. Geodite takes up a lot of room: You''re going to need a big cargo hold, or you''ll have to make several trips. </span'),
(57826,'/h2> Looks like there was some kind of explosion on a colony in this system, and thousands of people are without a home. I want you to take some of them over to the destination so we can do our part in providing shelter for less fortunate people. </span'),
(57855,'/h2> Looks like there was some kind of explosion on a colony in this system, and thousands of people are without a home. I want you to take some of them over to the destination so we can do our part in providing shelter for less fortunate people. </span'),
(57856,'/h2> Bio-engineers and farmers in nearby settlements, which have been supplying us with foodstuffs, have had good fortune recently. Their supplies of frozen plant seeds are overflowing, and they would like to sell some of their excess products. Obviously we took advantage of a good opportunity and bought the goods for silly prices, those people are so gullible. I''d like you to deliver the goods to the destination, where we''ve found a buyer. </span'),
(57882,'/h2> Bio-engineers and farmers in nearby settlements, which have been supplying us with foodstuffs, have had good fortune recently. Their supplies of frozen plant seeds are overflowing, and they would like to sell some of their excess products. Obviously we took advantage of a good opportunity and bought the goods for silly prices, those people are so gullible. I''d like you to deliver the goods to the destination, where we''ve found a buyer. </span'),
(60117,'/h2> I just received news of a very grave incident that just occured in the system the dungeon''s system a few hours ago. A convoy carrying our esteemed CEO was ambushed by an unusually large and organized pirate strike force. But fortune shone on us tonight, for due to the extraordinary bravery of our CEOs valiant escort team, he managed to escape unharmed, although slightly traumatised as you might expect. We lost many good men in this unfortunate incident, including the commander of our escort team ... may he rest in peace. Now I''ll get right to the point. We believe the pirates managed to capture some of the crew of the cruiser which was escorting our CEO, as we found the wreckage of their ship close by the encounter location, lacking the bodies of most of the crew. the faction special forces have been called in and are scouring the area for any traces left behind by the pirates, which so far remain at large. We''d like you to help out in the investigation. We know of a popular pirate hideout in the dungeon''s system, please search the area for any clues left behind. </span'),
(60065,'/h2> Our intelligence team has just informed us of fresh new evidence, which apparently points to the girl being held in a Serpentis stronghold in the dungeon''s system. According to our sources she is being held in the Central Hub structure of the base, where she will be executed if their demands aren''t met. It is our civic duty to see to it that she is returned to her family safely before those despicable Serpentis villains murder her. There is a fundamental flaw with our plan however, the Serpentis are fully aware of our intention to free her and have sent in a fleet of their battleships to guard their outpost. Now I certainly do not expect you to fight against such odds, but I firmly believe you capable of infiltrating their base, rescuing the girl and escaping with your ship, and life, intact. We have located a series of acceleration gates leading straight to the Central Control Hub. The Serpentis fleet guarding it will be expecting a large force of attackers, which will give you the advantage should you fly in there with a fast, agile ship, to avoid direct confrontation. Once you arrive at the final area, all you have to do is destroy the Central Control Hub and retrieve the girl from the ejected safety capsule, all of their Control Hubs have this mechanism to save their high-ranking personnel from death should the structure be obliterated. We hope that they consider the girl important enough to save in this way as well. If not ... well there is not much other choice. If we send in a fleet of ships they will simply kill her when they realize they have lost. We need to hit them fast and hard, before they know what hit them. That is the only chance we have of getting her out of there alive. Now, if you do not find the girl alive after destroying the Central Control Hub, then active your warp drive immediately and get out of there! I wouldn''t want to lose you needlessly, you. But rest assured, should you fall then I will personally make sure the pirate scum pay the price. Good luck. </span'),
(60118,'/h2> After checking our logs we noticed that only some of the prisoners you brought back were part of the crew that was captured after the pirate raid on our convoy. The rest apparently are former members of one of the pirate ships you destroyed, who managed to escape from the blast that destroyed their vessel. I need them transfered to some colleagues of mine at another station for further interrogation, hopefully the specialists there will be able to extract out of them the information we need to track down who was behind the ambush on our CEO. </span'),
(60119,'/h2> We need urgent help with intercepting a group of vile kidnappers who just managed to snatch the niece of our CEO while she was visiting her uncle in this very system. We believe the perpetrators were a gang of mercenaries led by a felon working for the illegal organization, the Odamian Renegades. I''ll fill you in on the details of that organization in your mission details. What I need you to do is capture this agent of theirs, alive if possible. We must have him here for interrogation, as we suspect he is the missing link between the kidnapping and those who are truly responsible for this heinous crime. We need to get to the bottom of which organization stands behind these grave assaults against our people. And it so happens that we know the whereabouts of a certain pirate who has had many dealings with this Odamian agent in the past, who we hope will be able to lead you to him. The only catch is he will most likely require a bit of ''convincing'' on your part before he parts with the needed information. I''ll upload the bookmark to his location into your NeoCom, once you have extracted the information from the middleman then I expect you to find the Odamian agent and bring him back to me. </span'),
(60120,'/h2> While we wait for the interrogation of the prisoner you captured in your last mission to finish, I''d like you to transport a data chip that we retrieved from his belongings to the destination. We''d like it decyphered and I know of the perfect man for the job, who is residing on that station. We aren''t sure if there is any incriminating evidence in the data, but we''d like to make sure nonetheless. When you get back, then hopefully our interrogators will have found some more leads. </span'),
(60121,'/h2> Yes, the interrogation went well. We managed to extract out of him who he was working for. Apparently he had been contacted by an agent from the Odamian Renegades, a criminal organization which has been making quite a name for itself recently in these parts, and paid a vast sum of money to kidnap our CEO''s niece. A foolhardy task, but he did manage to pull it off and transfer her into the hands of the criminals. Also the data disc you transported in your last mission has revealed even more to us. It contained the precise meeting points between the kidnappers and the Odamian agent for the past few weeks, as well as the exact coordinates for the next meeting which is to take place any minute now. I''d like you to fly over there yourself and ambush the Odamian goons at that location. Try to be quick, I don''t know how long they will stay there waiting for their contact to arrive. </span'),
(60122,'/h2> We have a major flu outbreak here on the agent''s station. Because of this our antiviral drug supplies have grown thin, and we''re afraid we''ll run out soon. We have a lot of personnel here, we wouldn''t want half of them taking sick leave due to our lack of medicines. I ordered the purchase of some antiviral drugs at the pickup location and would like you to transport them here. Please hurry, our staff is depending on you. </span'),
(60123,'/h2> Very interesting indeed. You''ve done us a good service, you. Now let''s just hope that these Serpentis scoundrels can reveal the true location of our CEO''s niece. </span'),
(60063,'/h2> A Serpentis strike force was spotted entering this system earlier today, wiping out some of our patrol ships in a surprise assault! We received a distress signal, only moments ago, coming from one of our civilian convoys traveling towards a supply depot in the dungeon, it has been attacked by these pirate forces. Please undock immediately and fly to their rescue, before it''s too late! I''ll supply you with a bookmark to their exact coordinates. Now hurry! </span'),
(60064,'/h2> While we were scrambling to defend our convoys from attacks by the Serpentis, a few of their agents broke into our prison module and managed to escape with the prisoners. Our interrogation of them was not complete, we still don''t know where their base is located, so we are quite desperate to get them back here. We know where their ships are headed, and we request that you intercept them before they manage to jump out of this system. This might be our last chance of getting them before they vanish into deep space, so please hurry! </span'),
(60012,'/h2> While examining wrecked rogue drones following a failed attack, strange minerals were found which replaced some of the drones'' usual systems. The compounds seem to run more efficiently than the parts they replaced, and your agent has hired you to take the find to researchers for examination. </span'),
(60029,'/h2> While examining wrecked rogue drones following a failed attack, strange minerals were found which replaced some of the drones'' usual systems. The compounds seem to run more efficiently than the parts they replaced, and your agent has hired you to take the find to researchers for examination. </span'),
(60051,'/h2> While examining wrecked rogue drones following a failed attack, strange minerals were found which replaced some of the drones'' usual systems. The compounds seem to run more efficiently than the parts they replaced, and your agent has hired you to take the find to researchers for examination. </span'),
(60095,'/h2> Fly out to the dungeon and clear the area for the humanitarian convoy. </span'),
(90012,'/h2> My superiors over at the destination are waiting for these reports. I''m swamped with work so I need you to deliver them for me. Don''t mess this up. Both our jobs are on the line here. </span'),
(90041,'/h2> My superiors over at the destination are waiting for these reports. I''m swamped with work so I need you to deliver them for me. Don''t mess this up. Both our jobs are on the line here. </span'),
(90062,'/h2> My superiors over at the destination are waiting for these reports. I''m swamped with work so I need you to deliver them for me. Don''t mess this up. Both our jobs are on the line here. </span'),
(90082,'/h2> My superiors over at the destination are waiting for these reports. I''m swamped with work so I need you to deliver them for me. Don''t mess this up. Both our jobs are on the line here. </span'),
(90013,'/h2> Homeless people are everywhere, littering the streets. I''ve gathered up a whole bunch of them, and I want you to go and dump them at the destination. Make it somebody else''s problem! </span'),
(90042,'/h2> Homeless people are everywhere, littering the streets. I''ve gathered up a whole bunch of them, and I want you to go and dump them at the destination. Make it somebody else''s problem! </span'),
(90063,'/h2> Homeless people are everywhere, littering the streets. I''ve gathered up a whole bunch of them, and I want you to go and dump them at the destination. Make it somebody else''s problem! </span'),
(56911,'/h2> The Crackpot has been hiding his heretical nonsense in copies of the Pax Amarria! This is absolutely intolerable! Needless to say, we''ve been seizing copies as they''re found, and of course those in possession of such an insulting piece of work have been detained for questioning. Still, that leaves us with a pile of gilded filth on our hands. I want you to go pick up the copies that are being held and bring them back here. We''re having the Pax Amarria covers stripped off before we send them along for the ceremonial burning. </span'),
(56912,'/h2> We''ve finally got The Crackpot. I need you to go pick him up and bring him here. We''ve made sure to keep him anonymous. Go and get him before some other loon tries to break him out. </span'),
(58083,'/h2> A team of mercenaries led by a man calling himself “Black Dog” has killed one of our senior managers as he toured an asteroid field not far from here. Intelligence has indicated that he intends to continue these operations into the foreseeable future. To remedy this unacceptable situation, we need you to transport a trained assassin and his entourage to a station closer to the scene of the crime. Once this is done, you will have completed the terms of this contract. We appreciate your discretion in this endeavor. </span'),
(58118,'/h2> A team of mercenaries led by a man calling himself “Black Dog” has killed one of our senior managers as he toured an asteroid field not far from here. Intelligence has indicated that he intends to continue these operations into the foreseeable future. To remedy this unacceptable situation, we need you to transport a trained assassin and his entourage to a station closer to the scene of the crime. Once this is done, you will have completed the terms of this contract. We appreciate your discretion in this endeavor. </span'),
(56923,'/h2> Mine 20 units of Crystalline Icicles. Oh, and watch out for pirates or rogue drones. Lots of them around these parts. You will need an Ice Harvester module to complete this mission. Also, be aware that this amount of raw Crystalline Icicles ore may require multiple trips unless you have a large amount of cargo space. </span'),
(91020,'/h2> Mine 20 units of Crystalline Icicles. Oh, and watch out for pirates or rogue drones. Lots of them around these parts. You will need an Ice Harvester module to complete this mission. Also, be aware that this amount of raw Crystalline Icicles ore may require multiple trips unless you have a large amount of cargo space. </span'),
(60085,'/h2> An Amarrian slaver has found a way to hack the Egonics signal, at least at short range. Security cameras in a nearby station show hundreds of people--all of them wearing Egonics devices--simply walking into the cargohold of an Amarrian Bestower. It wasn''t until after the ship had departed the station and the missing persons reports starting coming in that we realized anything was amiss. Security found that this Amarrian "citizen" had inserted subliminal commands into the Egonics signals at the station. If you can get all of those citizens back, there''s a big reward for you. There are over 1,000 people missing. You will need a large cargo capacity to carry them all at once, unless you intend to make multiple runs to the deadspace location where the Amarrain ship is located. </span'),
(60096,'/h2> The Gallente have set up another mining operation near one of our asteroid belts. They bring in semi-mobile reprocessing stations and then mine the location dry. You have to recognize this as just another act of war, you. the agent''s corporation has lost millions of ISK to these Federation parasites. It''s almost as damaging as a direct attack, but it doesn''t draw the sort of military response an overt assault would, which is why we need capsuleer assistance to deal with this quickly. We know they''ve set up mining outpost at one of the smaller deadspace asteroid pockets the agent''s corporation frequents. They do this in the hope that nobody will come after them. I need you to send the Federation a message that they''re wrong – that the State will pursue them every time. You must show them that there''s no profit to be made from illegally mining belts we have claimed. Go to the outpost and destroy absolutely everything; all the miners and any reprocessing stations you see. Level the place entirely. The loss of personnel and equipment will set them back and send a clear message to stick to their own space. </span'),
(57860,'/h2> We are launching one of our new listening posts nearby. Everything is ready and we have a Go signal from the authorities, but the idiots next door forgot to make sure they had the necessary supplies for the launch. We need you to ferry some rocket fuel so these baboons don''t lose their heads to the management. </span'),
(57894,'/h2> We are launching one of our new listening posts nearby. Everything is ready and we have a Go signal from the authorities, but the idiots next door forgot to make sure they had the necessary supplies for the launch. We need you to ferry some rocket fuel so these baboons don''t lose their heads to the management. </span'),
(57828,'/h2> A convoy of the agent''s corporation ships stumbled upon a stash of viral agents in the objective system while passing through the system. They dropped it off here so that a specialist can take a look at it and perhaps trace it to a particular individual or corporation. Now that they''re done, I need you to take it to the destination for further research. Don''t worry about getting busted by customs for transporting the viral agents: We''ve cleared the matter with them and they''ll be expecting you. </span'),
(57862,'/h2> A convoy of the agent''s corporation ships stumbled upon a stash of viral agents in the objective system while passing through the system. They dropped it off here so that a specialist can take a look at it and perhaps trace it to a particular individual or corporation. Now that they''re done, I need you to take it to the destination for further research. Don''t worry about getting busted by customs for transporting the viral agents: We''ve cleared the matter with them and they''ll be expecting you. </span'),
(60097,'/h2> Only a few moments ago the CEO from one of our subsidiaries was attacked and ransomed by Guristas, right in front of our trade delegation. Local security forces were overwhelmed and the pirates managed to escape. Our scouts pursued the Guristas vessels back to a Federation detention facility, which suggests the Guristas are only acting as mercenaries and the Gallente are really the ones to blame. We have scouts holding above the detention facility, and they''re tapping communications to look for evidence of a connection, but in the meantime we want to make an attempt to get our people out using capsuleer assistance. We''re concerned that more reinforcements could be on the way, and that if they arrive, we''ll lose our people for good. You need to act quickly. Your assignment is to assault the facility and return our people to us before things escalate any further. </span'),
(60098,'/h2> A convoy belonging to the Zainou Biotech corporation has broadcast a distress call to all nearby stations, saying they are under attack by unknown hostiles and going down fast. Because the convoy''s cargo, chemical components of an insorum prototype, is such a valuable and dangerous one, the CEP itself has given orders for all nearby agents to find ships capable of rescuing the cargo, even if the ships in the convoy are otherwise unsalvageable. You will need to fly to the last reported location of the convoy, eliminate the attacking vessels, and either escort the convoy to safety or recover the insorum components from the wreckage if it is already too late. It is imperative that this be taken care of as soon as possible; we cannot allow this cargo to fall into the wrong hands. You will need a Salvager to complete this task. </span'),
(60099,'/h2> Apparently, a rival corporation is afraid of our rapid growth in the field of starship design. An “associate” of ours has informed us that a shipment of datacores heading to one of our research stations is to be intercepted by a fleet of Guristas mercenaries. What''s disturbing is that an Amarr corporation has allegedly hired the pirates to do this dirty work. We want you to intercept and eliminate the Guristas threat. What we need is proof that our rivals are pulling their strings or that they have nothing to do with this whatsoever. </span'),
(57863,'/h2> As you know, keeping the grunts happy is one of my most important jobs. If they stop working, everything breaks down and we don''t want that. So, for the sake my head and yours, please ferry this shipment of tobacco to the the destination station. </span'),
(57896,'/h2> As you know, keeping the grunts happy is one of my most important jobs. If they stop working, everything breaks down and we don''t want that. So, for the sake my head and yours, please ferry this shipment of tobacco to the the destination station. </span'),
(60124,'/h2> I just received news of a grave incident that occurred in the dungeon''s system a few hours ago. A convoy carrying our esteemed CEO was ambushed by an unusually large and organized pirate strike force. But fortune shone on us tonight, for due to the extraordinary bravery of our CEO''s valiant escort team, he managed to escape unharmed, although slightly traumatised as you might expect. We lost many good men in this unfortunate incident, including the commander of our escort team ... may he rest in peace. Now, I''ll get right to the point. We believe the pirates managed to capture some of the crew of the cruiser that was escorting our CEO, for we found the wreckage of their ship close by the encounter location, but there was no trace of the bodies of most of the crew. Amarr Empire special forces have been called in and are scouring the area for any sign left behind by the pirates, who so far remain at large. We''d like you to help out in the investigation. We know of a popular pirate hideout in the dungeon''s system. I´ll upload the coordinates to your NeoCom: Please search the area for any clues, and if you take any prisoners, bring them back for interrogation. </span'),
(60068,'/h2> Our intelligence team has just informed us of new evidence that apparently points to the girl being held in a Blood Raider stronghold in the dungeon''s system. According to our information, she is being held in their chapel and is going to be sacrificed in the near future in one of their bloody rituals. We must see that she is returned to her family safely before those despicable Blood Raider fanatics murder her. There is a fundamental problem, however; the Blood Raiders are fully aware of our intention to free her and have sent in a fleet of their battleships to guard their outpost. Now, I certainly do not expect you to fight against such odds, but I firmly believe you capable of infiltrating their base, rescuing the girl, and escaping with your ship intact. We have located a series of acceleration gates leading straight to the chapel. Once you arrive at the final room, all you have to do is destroy the chapel and retrieve the girl from the ejected safety capsule. (All of their chapels have this mechanism in place to save their priests from death should the structure be obliterated.) If we send in a fleet of ships, the Blood Raiders will simply kill her as soon as they realize they have lost. We need to hit them fast and hard, with a small force, before they know what hit them. That is the only chance we have of getting her out of there alive. Now, if you do not find the girl alive after destroying the chapel, then active your warp drive immediately and get out of there! I wouldn''t want to lose you needlessly, you. But rest assured, should you fall, then I will personally make sure the Raider scum pay the price. Good luck. </span'),
(60125,'/h2> After checking our logs, we noticed that only some of the prisoners you brought back were part of the crew that was captured after the pirate raid on our convoy. The rest apparently are former members of one of the pirate ships you destroyed, who managed to escape from the blast that destroyed their vessel. I need them transferred to some colleagues of mine at another station for further interrogation; hopefully the specialists there will be able to extract the information we need to track down who was behind the ambush on our CEO. </span'),
(60126,'/h2> We urgently need help intercepting a group of kidnappers who just managed to snatch the niece of our CEO while she was visiting her uncle in this very system. We believe the perpetrators were a gang of mercenaries led by a felon working for an illegal organization called the Darkonnen. I''ll fill you in on the details of that organization in the mission details in your Opportunities interface. What I need you to do is capture this agent of theirs, alive if possible. We must have him here for interrogation, for we suspect he is the missing link between the kidnapping and those who are truly responsible for this heinous crime. We need to get to the bottom of which organization stands behind these grave assaults against our people. And it so happens that we know the whereabouts of a certain pirate who has had many dealings with a Darkonnen agent in the past; we hope this pirate will be able to lead you to the agent. The only catch is that he will most likely require a bit of "convincing" on your part before he parts with the needed information. I''ll upload the bookmark to his location into your NeoCom; once you have extracted the information from the middleman, I expect you to find the Darkonnen agent and bring him back to me. </span'),
(60127,'/h2> While we wait for the interrogation of the prisoner you captured, I''d like you to transport a data chip we retrieved from his belongings to the destination. We need it deciphered, and I happen to know the perfect man for the job, who lives at that station. We aren''t sure if there is any incriminating evidence in the data, but we''d like to make sure nonetheless. By the time you get back, I expect our interrogators will have found some more leads. </span'),
(60128,'/h2> Yes, the interrogation went well. We managed to find out who he was working for. Apparently he had been contacted by a Darkonnen agent and paid a vast sum of money to kidnap our CEO''s niece. A foolhardy task, but he did manage to pull it off and transfer her into the hands of the criminals. Also, the data disc you transported in your last mission has revealed even more to us. It contained the precise meeting points between the kidnappers and the Darkonnen agent for the past few weeks, as well as the exact coordinates for the next meeting, which is to take place very soon now. I''d like you to fly over there yourself and ambush the Darkonnen goons at that location. Be quick: I don''t know how long they will wait for their contact to arrive. </span'),
(60129,'/h2> We''ve had a major influenza outbreak here on the agent''s station. Because of it, our antiviral drug supplies have grown thin, and we''re afraid we''ll run out soon. We have a lot of personnel here; given the current state of affairs, we wouldn''t want half of them taking sick leave due to our lack of medicine. I''ve taken the liberty of ordering the purchase of some antiviral drugs at the pickup location; I need you to transport them here. Please hurry ― our staff is depending on you. </span'),
(60130,'/h2> I just received an anonymous transmission asking me to send you specifically to a meeting place in the dungeon''s system. It also said that the person you are to meet there has information that could be vital to our investigation of the disappearance of our CEO''s niece. I''m reluctant to send you, since this may be a trap, but I really have no choice. If I send someone else, though, I could be compromising the investigation. So I ask you, please head out to the bookmarked location which was given to me through the anonymous transmission. Be sure to record anything said to you and save it into your ship''s database, and then return with it to me. </span'),
(60066,'/h2> A Blood Raider strike force entered this system earlier today and wiped out some of our patrol ships in a surprise assault! Now we''ve received a broken distress signal, only moments ago, from one of our civilian convoys traveling to a supply depot in the dungeon. I fear it has been attacked by these same pirate forces. Please undock immediately and get over there before it''s too late! I''ll supply you with a bookmark to their exact coordinates. Now hurry! </span'),
(60067,'/h2> As I''ve already mentioned, while we were scrambling to defend our convoys from the Blood Raiders, a few of their agents broke into our prison module and managed to escape with your prisoners. Our interrogation was not complete and we still don''t know where their base is located, so we must get them back. We know where their ships are headed, though, and we need you to intercept them before they manage to jump out of this system. This might be our last chance of getting them before they vanish into deep space, so please hurry! </span'),
(90014,'/h2> My friend is getting married. We need entertainment for his bachelor party tomorrow, but I can''t just show up with the dancers myself. Take these "performers" to the destination for me. Be sure to get them there on time so we can start the fun! </span'),
(90043,'/h2> My friend is getting married. We need entertainment for his bachelor party tomorrow, but I can''t just show up with the dancers myself. Take these "performers" to the destination for me. Be sure to get them there on time so we can start the fun! </span'),
(90064,'/h2> My friend is getting married. We need entertainment for his bachelor party tomorrow, but I can''t just show up with the dancers myself. Take these "performers" to the destination for me. Be sure to get them there on time so we can start the fun! </span'),
(90083,'/h2> My friend is getting married. We need entertainment for his bachelor party tomorrow, but I can''t just show up with the dancers myself. Take these "performers" to the destination for me. Be sure to get them there on time so we can start the fun! </span'),
(60101,'/h2> Fly to the the dungeon system and obtain the salvaged electronics, then return them to your agent in the agent''s station. Destroy any Angel Cartel ships that get in the way. </span'),
(57114,'/h2> We''ve got a shipment of vaccines that need to be delivered to the destination in a hurry. I''m willing to provide a substantial bonus if they''re delivered right away. Regardless, the meds need to be delivered soon, though. Be sure to move the medicine into your cargo hold before you set out. And note the hasty delivery required — you don''t have much time! </span'),
(90015,'/h2> We''ve got a shipment of vaccines that need to be delivered to the destination in a hurry. I''m willing to provide a substantial bonus if they''re delivered right away. Regardless, the meds need to be delivered soon, though. Be sure to move the medicine into your cargo hold before you set out. And note the hasty delivery required — you don''t have much time! </span'),
(56878,'/h2> We''ve gotten word of the location of a bunch of Mercium ore here in the dungeon, but we believe that our information has also been leaked to other factions, including the Gallenteans. It''s vital that you collect all the Mercium: It cannot be allowed to fall into enemy hands. Be aware that this amount of raw Mercium ore may require multiple trips unless you have a large amount of cargo space. </span'),
(56879,'/h2> We''ve gotten word of the location of a bunch of Mercium ore here in the dungeon, but we believe that our information has also been leaked to other factions, including the Gallenteans. It''s vital that you collect all the Mercium: It cannot be allowed to fall into enemy hands. Be aware that this amount of raw Mercium ore may require multiple trips unless you have a large amount of cargo space. </span'),
(56880,'/h2> We''ve gotten word of the location of a bunch of Mercium ore here in the dungeon, but we believe that our information has also been leaked to other factions, including the Gallenteans. It''s vital that you collect all the Mercium: It cannot be allowed to fall into enemy hands. Be aware that this amount of raw Mercium ore may require multiple trips unless you have a large amount of cargo space. </span'),
(58553,'/h2> We''ve gotten word of the location of a bunch of Mercium ore here in the dungeon, but we believe that our information has also been leaked to other factions, including the Gallenteans. It''s vital that you collect all the Mercium: It cannot be allowed to fall into enemy hands. Be aware that this amount of raw Mercium ore may require multiple trips unless you have a large amount of cargo space. </span'),
(91007,'/h2> We''ve gotten word of the location of a bunch of Mercium ore here in the dungeon, but we believe that our information has also been leaked to other factions, including the Gallenteans. It''s vital that you collect all the Mercium: It cannot be allowed to fall into enemy hands. Be aware that this amount of raw Mercium ore may require multiple trips unless you have a large amount of cargo space. </span'),
(91003,'/h2> There''s a rich deposit of Mercium in this system. Bring me 1,800 units and we might both end up rich. </span'),
(55187,'/h2> We were ordered by high ranking officials in the faction to deliver a batch of Zemnar to the inhabitants of the destination. Their supplies are low and they need some backup incase of a viral outbreak. </span'),
(57990,'/h2> We were ordered by high ranking officials in the faction to deliver a batch of Zemnar to the inhabitants of the destination. Their supplies are low and they need some backup incase of a viral outbreak. </span'),
(90016,'/h2> We were ordered by high ranking officials in the faction to deliver a batch of Zemnar to the inhabitants of the destination. Their supplies are low and they need some backup incase of a viral outbreak. </span'),
(90044,'/h2> We were ordered by high ranking officials in the faction to deliver a batch of Zemnar to the inhabitants of the destination. Their supplies are low and they need some backup incase of a viral outbreak. </span'),
(90065,'/h2> We were ordered by high ranking officials in the faction to deliver a batch of Zemnar to the inhabitants of the destination. Their supplies are low and they need some backup incase of a viral outbreak. </span'),
(90084,'/h2> We were ordered by high ranking officials in the faction to deliver a batch of Zemnar to the inhabitants of the destination. Their supplies are low and they need some backup incase of a viral outbreak. </span'),
(56927,'/h2> We''ve located some asteroids that contain substantial amounts of Polygypsum — that''s a comparatively rare mineral, and almost completely unknown in this system. Our guys want to have a look at the stuff and see if they can figure out some way to make use of it; however, we don''t have anyone who wants to deal with it. So guess who I thought of first? You''ll need to grab all 2,800 units of the stuff and get it back here. See you then. </span'),
(91021,'/h2> We''ve located some asteroids that contain substantial amounts of Polygypsum — that''s a comparatively rare mineral, and almost completely unknown in this system. Our guys want to have a look at the stuff and see if they can figure out some way to make use of it; however, we don''t have anyone who wants to deal with it. So guess who I thought of first? You''ll need to grab all 2,800 units of the stuff and get it back here. See you then. </span'),
(90017,'/h2> the agent''s corporation needs these sealed cargo containers moved to the destination in a jiffy. Are you up for the job, you? </span'),
(90045,'/h2> the agent''s corporation needs these sealed cargo containers moved to the destination in a jiffy. Are you up for the job, you? </span'),
(90066,'/h2> the agent''s corporation needs these sealed cargo containers moved to the destination in a jiffy. Are you up for the job, you? </span'),
(90085,'/h2> the agent''s corporation needs these sealed cargo containers moved to the destination in a jiffy. Are you up for the job, you? </span'),
(54833,'/h2> A couple of our personnel here in Nonni require a lift. They need to be at the destination system for a meeting at the Mercantile Club. Please, don''t be late! </span'),
(60102,'/h2> Wipe out the Sansha hijackers in the dungeon. The more humiliating, the better. </span'),
(91022,'/h2> Demand for minerals is skyrocketing. Which is good for us. More demand means more profit. To fill that demand, though, we''re having to turn to some unorthodox ores: Green Arisite, for instance. I know of a large field that''s full of the stuff. If you can get it for me, I''ll make sure you''re reimbursed. We just may be able to make some use of it, with the right tech. Who knows? </span'),
(60013,'/h2> Some decades ago, Amarr veterinary scientists achieved a milestone in genetic manipulation with the creation of hybrid slaver hounds. These new breeds are specifically designed to live and work in extreme climate conditions, which is a boon for all those slave labor facilities on ice planets and other harsh environments. Demand for these animals has been overwhelming and we are struggling to maintain our delivery schedule. I need a large shipment of these hybrid slaver hounds delivered to a nearby station. From there they will be transshipped to a desert planet and put to work as guard animals. </span'),
(60014,'/h2> A small, platoon-sized Caldari special operation team is in hiding on a Gallente planet and in danger of being captured or killed. They are low on water, food, weapons, and other equipment and will not last long unless they are extracted. We have a rescue standing by; however, we need you to deliver the required materials to their station so that they can then proceed with this critical rescue mission. </span'),
(58084,'/h2> One of our R&amp;D facilities has been working hard to produce a new type of cloaking device for Covert Ops vessels that will allow those ships to remain cloaked while jumping stargates. However, it has recently been brought to our attention that a corporate espionage agent sent by a rival company is targeting this new technology, for obvious reasons. In order to flush him out and arrest him, however, we need to catch him in the act. So, we are asking you to transport a decoy prototype cloaking device from this station to one we designate. With such a juicy target, we feel the spy will not be able to resist making an attempt to steal it somewhere between here and there. We need you to fly this device to that station utilizing absolute secrecy. </span'),
(58120,'/h2> One of our R&amp;D facilities has been working hard to produce a new type of cloaking device for Covert Ops vessels that will allow those ships to remain cloaked while jumping stargates. However, it has recently been brought to our attention that a corporate espionage agent sent by a rival company is targeting this new technology, for obvious reasons. In order to flush him out and arrest him, however, we need to catch him in the act. So, we are asking you to transport a decoy prototype cloaking device from this station to one we designate. With such a juicy target, we feel the spy will not be able to resist making an attempt to steal it somewhere between here and there. We need you to fly this device to that station utilizing absolute secrecy. </span'),
(60016,'/h2> One of our R&amp;D facilities has been working hard to produce a new type of cloaking device for Covert Ops vessels that will allow those ships to remain cloaked while jumping stargates. However, it has recently been brought to our attention that a corporate espionage agent sent by a rival company is targeting this new technology, for obvious reasons. In order to flush him out and arrest him, however, we need to catch him in the act. So, we are asking you to transport a decoy prototype cloaking device from this station to one we designate. With such a juicy target, we feel the spy will not be able to resist making an attempt to steal it somewhere between here and there. We need you to fly this device to that station utilizing absolute secrecy. </span'),
(60015,'/h2> In order to get around the laws pertaining to the transportation of illegal drugs through Amarr Empire space, we have been forced to create new and unknown substances for use on, or by, rather, our various slave labor enclaves. This new drug, Blue Paradise, does away with many of the harmful chemicals previously used while actually increasing the pleasurable effects. We are certain that, properly controlled and distributed, introduction of this drug into the slave labor workforce will increase productivity by a substantial margin. We are counting on you to deliver it to the designation transshipment station as soon as possible. </span'),
(60030,'/h2> In order to get around the laws pertaining to the transportation of illegal drugs through Amarr Empire space, we have been forced to create new and unknown substances for use on, or by, rather, our various slave labor enclaves. This new drug, Blue Paradise, does away with many of the harmful chemicals previously used while actually increasing the pleasurable effects. We are certain that, properly controlled and distributed, introduction of this drug into the slave labor workforce will increase productivity by a substantial margin. We are counting on you to deliver it to the designation transshipment station as soon as possible. </span'),
(60052,'/h2> In order to get around the laws pertaining to the transportation of illegal drugs through Amarr Empire space, we have been forced to create new and unknown substances for use on, or by, rather, our various slave labor enclaves. This new drug, Blue Paradise, does away with many of the harmful chemicals previously used while actually increasing the pleasurable effects. We are certain that, properly controlled and distributed, introduction of this drug into the slave labor workforce will increase productivity by a substantial margin. We are counting on you to deliver it to the designation transshipment station as soon as possible. </span'),
(55192,'/h2> To eliminate the depressive mood of our hangar staff, cargo bay workers, janitors and other laborers we decided to throw them a party at the destination. I''d like you to do the honors of delivering the spiced wine to the gathering. And don''t forget, a quick delivery will get you a bonus! </span'),
(57916,'/h2> To eliminate the depressive mood of our hangar staff, cargo bay workers, janitors and other laborers we decided to throw them a party at the destination. I''d like you to do the honors of delivering the spiced wine to the gathering. And don''t forget, a quick delivery will get you a bonus! </span'),
(90018,'/h2> To eliminate the depressive mood of our hangar staff, cargo bay workers, janitors and other laborers we decided to throw them a party at the destination. I''d like you to do the honors of delivering the spiced wine to the gathering. And don''t forget, a quick delivery will get you a bonus! </span'),
(90046,'/h2> To eliminate the depressive mood of our hangar staff, cargo bay workers, janitors and other laborers we decided to throw them a party at the destination. I''d like you to do the honors of delivering the spiced wine to the gathering. And don''t forget, a quick delivery will get you a bonus! </span'),
(90067,'/h2> To eliminate the depressive mood of our hangar staff, cargo bay workers, janitors and other laborers we decided to throw them a party at the destination. I''d like you to do the honors of delivering the spiced wine to the gathering. And don''t forget, a quick delivery will get you a bonus! </span'),
(90086,'/h2> To eliminate the depressive mood of our hangar staff, cargo bay workers, janitors and other laborers we decided to throw them a party at the destination. I''d like you to do the honors of delivering the spiced wine to the gathering. And don''t forget, a quick delivery will get you a bonus! </span'),
(60103,'/h2> A drone network virus seems has taken over a mining colony and is infecting any ship that approaches. Eradicate all infected ships and destroy the virus before it infects yours. </span'),
(60104,'/h2> It appears the Gallente have been making hostile moves again in the the dungeon system. They''ve been continuously launching attacks from a command vessel somewhere in a deadspace pocket. Our scouts have located the Federation admiral responsible for these raids and now we just need her taken care of. We''ve dealt with this thing before, so we''re confident that removing her from the picture will disrupt the rest of the Gallente operations in our area. The only issue is that the Navy won''t be able to mobilize against her in time – they''re the Navy after all, not a hit squad. I''ve been asked to recruit a capsuleer if possible, so we can bypass internal military procedures altogether. That''s where you come in you. We need you to travel over to the dungeon, enter the deadspace pocket our scouts have found, then kill the commander and her fleet. She''ll undoubtedly be back at some point even if your mission is successful. The Gallente are a persistent enemy, so after you''ve killed her, leave the body in the communication array she''s been coordinating the forces out of. That should send a message. It might even spook her into seeking reassignment elsewhere, away from our corporation''s space. </span'),
(56913,'/h2> Our miners have just reported a bunch of rogue drones in the system. Between them and the damned ore thieves, I''m almost ready to give up. They''re worse than Gallentean greenroaches – if we don''t show them that they''re not welcome here, we''ll be up to our eyeballs. And I can''t send my guys out there if I know they might be in danger. No, we need a capsuleer on this job, someone capable of defending a ship and mining at the same time. I''ve bookmarked a mining site for you. Go on out there and, if you see any drones, take ''em out. You know the risks. Then mine whatever Banidine you find out there so I can find out what the damn things are so interested in. </span'),
(91013,'/h2> Our miners have just reported a bunch of rogue drones in the system. Between them and the damned ore thieves, I''m almost ready to give up. They''re worse than Gallentean greenroaches – if we don''t show them that they''re not welcome here, we''ll be up to our eyeballs. And I can''t send my guys out there if I know they might be in danger. No, we need a capsuleer on this job, someone capable of defending a ship and mining at the same time. I''ve bookmarked a mining site for you. Go on out there and, if you see any drones, take ''em out. You know the risks. Then mine whatever Banidine you find out there so I can find out what the damn things are so interested in. </span'),
(60017,'/h2> One of the agent''s corporation''s archaeological teams has uncovered a load of pre-Federation relics. I need you to transport the pieces to a laboratory for analysis. </span'),
(56920,'/h2> I''ve just discovered a sizable deposit of Pithix out by an old mining station. The station''s been abandoned for a while now, but there are still working sensors in the area; that''s how we picked up on the Pithix. Problem is, the transmission''s hardly secure. I need you to get out there and bring me back that rock before someone else cleans the place out. Oh, there might also be some rogue drone activity in the area. Fair warning. </span'),
(91014,'/h2> I''ve just discovered a sizable deposit of Pithix out by an old mining station. The station''s been abandoned for a while now, but there are still working sensors in the area; that''s how we picked up on the Pithix. Problem is, the transmission''s hardly secure. I need you to get out there and bring me back that rock before someone else cleans the place out. Oh, there might also be some rogue drone activity in the area. Fair warning. </span'),
(60086,'/h2> The "Brothers of Freedom" have set up an FTL transmitter in the area of the dungeon and are broadcasting anti-corporate propaganda into the State, with the help of some Minmatar sympathizers. This situation is completely unacceptable; the transmitter must be destroyed, and we want you take care of it. Eliminate the transmitter and any hostile ships nearby. If the Minmatar Navy interferes, you can take out their vessels as well, but it''s not strictly necessary. </span'),
(60105,'/h2> Go pick up the Caldari operative from the penal station in the dungeon and bring him back. </span'),
(60106,'/h2> A portion of the fleet is preparing a set of protracted war games in the next few days. There was some mix up with a circuitry order that I only just found out about. Collect the custom circuitry from the production line in the dungeon. The level of piracy in the area is unknown. </span'),
(60107,'/h2> A new race track is being built in the dungeon. During the final stages of building, we received reports of some ships bearing Gallente markings, and several suspicious "accidents" have occurred. Sabotage is suspected. Go find these ships and destroy them so that no harm will come to participants or viewers during the big race. </span'),
(55369,'/h2> I''d like you to do some reconnaissance for the agent''s corporation, my friend. Our operatives in an outpost within the dungeon have requested a convoy of goods, through some pretty hostile territory. There are a few routes we could take to reach the destination, and you''re going to help us find the safest route. All I need you to do is scout ahead and see if there are any pirates, rogue drones or dangerous terrain. Report your findings to me. I''ll upload a bookmark to the first area into your NeoCom. </span'),
(55420,'/h2> I''d like you to do some reconnaissance for the agent''s corporation, my friend. Our operatives in an outpost within the dungeon have requested a convoy of goods, through some pretty hostile territory. There are a few routes we could take to reach the destination, and you''re going to help us find the safest route. All I need you to do is scout ahead and see if there are any pirates, rogue drones or dangerous terrain. Report your findings to me. I''ll upload a bookmark to the first area into your NeoCom. </span'),
(60108,'/h2> A pirate faction in the the dungeon system has taken hostages and plan on executing them shortly. The innocent people need to be rescued and returned to the agent as soon as possible. </span'),
(80064,'/h2> I just discovered why that research team never arrived to pick up the goods you ferried: their labs are under siege by Guristas forces. I don''t know what the hell the Guristas think they''re going to achieve down here, but if we don''t quickly shut them down we risk them gaining a foothold. This attack was fierce and well-coordinated. They managed to overwhelm our defenses. All of our other forces are either too far away to assist or on other important missions they can''t be diverted from. You''re our best shot. I want you to save that research station from the Guristas assault. </span'),
(90019,'/h2> Have you seen the price of oil around here lately? It''s absurd! Our clients are demanding more, but all we''ve got is the synthetic stuff, so take a load of it over to the destination. </span'),
(90047,'/h2> Have you seen the price of oil around here lately? It''s absurd! Our clients are demanding more, but all we''ve got is the synthetic stuff, so take a load of it over to the destination. </span'),
(90068,'/h2> Have you seen the price of oil around here lately? It''s absurd! Our clients are demanding more, but all we''ve got is the synthetic stuff, so take a load of it over to the destination. </span'),
(90087,'/h2> Have you seen the price of oil around here lately? It''s absurd! Our clients are demanding more, but all we''ve got is the synthetic stuff, so take a load of it over to the destination. </span'),
(57992,'/h2> Deliver the secure coded package for your agent. </span'),
(90020,'/h2> Deliver the secure coded package for your agent. </span'),
(55194,'/h2> The local news recently aired a story on poor immigrants in the destination system. Apparently some of the families have fallen on hard times and lack the funds to even buy the most basic necessities. A few concerned citizens in the agent''s system asked me to have these clothes delivered to the needy in the destination system, which they can make use of. I''d like you to make the first leg of the trip, which is to drop off the goods at the destination. Officials at the station will take care of the rest. </span'),
(57917,'/h2> The local news recently aired a story on poor immigrants in the destination system. Apparently some of the families have fallen on hard times and lack the funds to even buy the most basic necessities. A few concerned citizens in the agent''s system asked me to have these clothes delivered to the needy in the destination system, which they can make use of. I''d like you to make the first leg of the trip, which is to drop off the goods at the destination. Officials at the station will take care of the rest. </span'),
(90021,'/h2> The local news recently aired a story on poor immigrants in the destination system. Apparently some of the families have fallen on hard times and lack the funds to even buy the most basic necessities. A few concerned citizens in the agent''s system asked me to have these clothes delivered to the needy in the destination system, which they can make use of. I''d like you to make the first leg of the trip, which is to drop off the goods at the destination. Officials at the station will take care of the rest. </span'),
