(57832,'/h2> the agent''s corporation is in the middle of constructing an outpost in the destination. Our engineers there claim to lack a few loads of construction blocks to finish the work, and I was asked to deliver some blocks to that station. Could you please take the material straight to the destination? Our people in the destination system will take care of retrieving them from your hangar there for the construction project. </span'),
(57878,'/h2> the agent''s corporation is in the middle of constructing an outpost in the destination. Our engineers there claim to lack a few loads of construction blocks to finish the work, and I was asked to deliver some blocks to that station. Could you please take the material straight to the destination? Our people in the destination system will take care of retrieving them from your hangar there for the construction project. </span'),
(56881,'/h2> We''ve found an old mining post in the dungeon. But, the thing is, we can''t find who used to own it: There are no records of its being built or even existing. It''s simply empty. No sign of anyone left there, dead or otherwise. Our initial investigation found extensive fire damage, gas leaks; you name it, it went wrong. Lots of explosive damage, though we can''t tell if that was accidental or intentional. And some marks... well, we just don''t know what could do that to metal. It''s damn creepy, that''s for sure. Anyway, near as we can tell, the miners were working on a large Lyavite deposit. They didn''t finish, because there''s still about 5,000 units of it at the site. Now, I know Lyavite isn''t the most popular rock, but nobody just leaves that much ore lying around. And besides, the brains at the lab figure they can use the stuff for some of their research, so this opportunity is too good to pass up. That''s where you come in. Warp in, mine the Lyavite, and warp out. It''s that easy. </span'),
(91008,'/h2> We''ve found an old mining post in the dungeon. But, the thing is, we can''t find who used to own it: There are no records of its being built or even existing. It''s simply empty. No sign of anyone left there, dead or otherwise. Our initial investigation found extensive fire damage, gas leaks; you name it, it went wrong. Lots of explosive damage, though we can''t tell if that was accidental or intentional. And some marks... well, we just don''t know what could do that to metal. It''s damn creepy, that''s for sure. Anyway, near as we can tell, the miners were working on a large Lyavite deposit. They didn''t finish, because there''s still about 5,000 units of it at the site. Now, I know Lyavite isn''t the most popular rock, but nobody just leaves that much ore lying around. And besides, the brains at the lab figure they can use the stuff for some of their research, so this opportunity is too good to pass up. That''s where you come in. Warp in, mine the Lyavite, and warp out. It''s that easy. </span'),
(60036,'/h2> During a high-level security assessment, a decoy maglev train designed to mimic the regional governor''s chartered train was destroyed by unknown saboteurs while traveling at very high speed. Our investigation has yet to uncover the traitors; however, we are confident that a prompt scientific examination of the wreckage will provide the clues we need to resolve this internal security matter. We are sending a team of senior investigators to the wreck site so that they might help determine the identities of the attackers. We are counting on you to fly them to the designated station. </span'),
(54351,'/h2> I have terrible news, you. A major personnel convoy carrying countless the faction members was completely obliterated by Blood Raider ships, led by that damned commander of theirs, Faramon Mundan. His reputation as a brutal Covenant military leader has traveled far and wide these past few years, and it''s time to put an end to his miserable existence. I want you to be the bringer of our vengeance, you. Strike him down like the dog he is. When his battleship has been turned to dust, then you shall receive your reward. </span'),
(54352,'/h2> I have terrible news, you. A major personnel convoy carrying countless the faction members was completely obliterated by Blood Raider ships, led by that damned commander of theirs, Faramon Mundan. His reputation as a brutal Covenant military leader has traveled far and wide these past few years, and it''s time to put an end to his miserable existence. I want you to be the bringer of our vengeance, you. Strike him down like the dog he is. When his battleship has been turned to dust, then you shall receive your reward. </span'),
(54581,'/h2> I have terrible news, you. A major personnel convoy carrying countless the faction members was completely obliterated by Blood Raider ships, led by that damned commander of theirs, Faramon Mundan. His reputation as a brutal Covenant military leader has traveled far and wide these past few years, and it''s time to put an end to his miserable existence. I want you to be the bringer of our vengeance, you. Strike him down like the dog he is. When his battleship has been turned to dust, then you shall receive your reward. </span'),
(60023,'/h2> I have to request a difficult task of you: play nice with a swarm of Angel Cartel representatives and their entourage on your ship. Hopefully they won''t try to cause you trouble. </span'),
(60114,'/h2> The Republic bastards just launched a daring but foolhardy attack on our outpost in the dungeon. They killed every man, woman and child residing there, taking no prisoners. This was probably a retaliatory attack after we killed one of their commanders, but it matters not. We must intercept them before it''s too late. I have reliable information that the leader of this attack was none other than Warlord Ixon Kruz, so you will undoubtedly have a very tough fight on your hands. Prepare yourself well, but don''t tarry too long or you won''t get there in time! </span'),
(90031,'/h2> On the loading dock is a shipment of weapons for our 412th Regiment, currently garrisoned at the destination. Can you get it there for them? Remember to move the High-Tech Small Arms to your cargo hold before departure. </span'),
(60020,'/h2> Federation R&amp;D specialists have been working to find counters for Caldari military tactics; the latest development is a special type of ammunition that works similarly to a lock breaker bomb, but on a single target. I want you to take it over to a navy base for testing, and you need to keep word of this development from going very far. </span'),
(60045,'/h2> Federation R&amp;D specialists have been working to find counters for Caldari military tactics; the latest development is a special type of ammunition that works similarly to a lock breaker bomb, but on a single target. I want you to take it over to a navy base for testing, and you need to keep word of this development from going very far. </span')
